{"query":"Do state or national Amber Alert records or missing-children clearinghouses list license plate Q72B381 in connection with an Amber Alert?","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.missingkids.org","snippet":"State Missing Person Clearinghouses (1-800-843-5678) number. Toll-Free Line: (800) 346-3243. Missing Children's Clearinghouse 804-674","title":"AMBER Alerts - MissingKids.org","url":"https://www.missingkids.org/gethelpnow/amber"},{"position":2,"site_name":"amberalert.ojp.gov","snippet":"AMBER plans require law enforcement to confirm an abduction prior to issuing an alert. This is essential when determining the level of risk to the child.","title":"Guidelines for Issuing AMBER Alerts - Office of Justice Programs","url":"https://amberalert.ojp.gov/about/guidelines-for-issuing-alerts"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.chp.ca.gov","snippet":"The WEA AMBER Alert notification is automatically sent from National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC) at the time of the AMBER Alert activation ...","title":"AMBER Alert Plan - California Highway Patrol - CA.gov","url":"https://www.chp.ca.gov/news-alerts/alerts/amber-alert-plan/"},{"position":4,"site_name":"www.rtdna.org","snippet":"It also might include information about potential suspects, including if they are a registered sex offender, as well as vehicle description and license plate.","title":"Amber Alerts - Radio Television Digital News Association","url":"https://www.rtdna.org/amber-alerts"},{"position":5,"site_name":"en.wikipedia.org","snippet":"Public information in an Amber alert usually includes the name and description of the abductee, and license plate number of the abductor's vehicle if available.","title":"Amber alert - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amber_alert"},{"position":6,"site_name":"amber.ny.gov","snippet":"Notify the NYS Division of Criminal Justice Services (DCJS) Missing Persons Clearinghouse, National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC), FBI ..."